From 734b9dcb6980f618505729c9a21f34fc1e5706c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?K=C3=A9vin=20R=C3=A9mondi=C3=A8re?= <kevin@localhost>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 18:35:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/57] server: grammar-compatible backend sampling (fast-path
 validation + raw-logits resample)

[TAG_GRAMMAR_BACKEND] common/sampling.cpp:448 used to hard-disable backend sampling
for grammar requests, pushing every tool-call generation onto the CPU sampler
(24.4 vs 32.0 t/s measured). Now the backend-sampled token is validated against
the grammar with a single-token check (~us) and, on rejection, a full-vocab CPU
resample runs mirroring the grammar_first=false rejection path:
- llama_get_raw_logits_ith: raw full-vocab logits, bypassing the ~20 sampled
  candidates that llama_get_logits_ith prefers in backend mode (the first
  implementation read past the candidates buffer and produced garbage)
- llama_sampler_chain_apply_cpu: apply all stages of a backend-initialized
  chain on the CPU (chain_apply skips backend stages once offloaded)
- llama_set_need_raw_logits: per-seq flag, forces the ~1 MB raw-logit download
  for grammar sequences (the only residual cost, -2.8% vs no-grammar)
Validated: temp-0 outputs byte-identical to the previous CPU path, grammar
decode 24.4 -> 31.1 t/s (+28%), no-grammar unchanged.
